  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EEI - US Geological Survey IAA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Development, Democracy, and Innovation (D):  The purpose of this program is to provide USAID Missions and USAID Washington with access to the specialized expertise represented within the United States Geological Survey (USGS) in environment and natural resources related to land use monitoring systems to achieve low emission land use and economic development. This program builds on ongoing USGS work to improve the capacity of developing countries to measure and monitor forest carbon and improve data on land cover change as part of the multi-agency SilvaCarbon program. This Agreement will provide an efficient mechanism for USAID Washington and Missions to engage the technical capabilities of the USGS to support measuring and monitoring land cover and land use change as well as other information related to integrating natural resource management with low emission development objectives. This interagency agreement accommodates mission buy-ins..</narrative>
  </description>
